{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q30647364","formula":"C₂₄H₂₉NO","hill":"C24H29NO","elements":["H","C","N","O"],"composition":{"C":24.0,"H":29.0,"N":1.0,"O":1.0},"names":{"en":"Δ4-abiraterone"},"descriptions":{"en":"Δ4-Abiraterone (D4A; code name CB-7627), also known as 17-(3-pyridyl)androsta-4,16-dien-3-one, is a steroidogenesis inhibitor and active metabolite of abiraterone acetate, a drug which is used in the treatment of prostate cancer and is itself a prodrug of abiraterone (another active metabolite of abiraterone acetate). D4A is formed from abiraterone by 3β-hydroxysteroid dehydrogenase/Δ5-4 isomerase (3β-HSD). It is said to be a more potent inhibitor of steroidogenesis than abiraterone, and is partially responsible for the activity of abiraterone acetate."},"fame":1,"pubchemCid":196941,"mass":347.5,"charge":0,"smiles":"C[C@]12CCC(=O)C=C1CC[C@@H]3[C@@H]2CC[C@]4([C@H]3CC=C4C5=CN=CC=C5)C","inchikey":"GYJZZAJJENTSTP-NHFPKVKZSA-N","iupac":"(8R,9S,10R,13S,14S)-10,13-dimethyl-17-pyridin-3-yl-1,2,6,7,8,9,11,12,14,15-decahydrocyclopenta[a]phenanthren-3-one","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"196941","atoms":55,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":6.657,"y":0.873,"z":1.413,"el":"O"},{"x":-5.491,"y":1.87,"z":-0.411,"el":"N"},{"x":0.876,"y":-1.141,"z":-0.378,"el":"C"},{"x":1.411,"y":0.278,"z":-0.007,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.569,"y":-1.253,"z":0.116,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.522,"y":-0.218,"z":-0.544,"el":"C"},{"x":2.909,"y":0.498,"z":-0.447,"el":"C"},{"x":0.443,"y":1.404,"z":-0.462,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.031,"y":1.162,"z":-0.077,"el":"C"},{"x":1.774,"y":-2.217,"z":0.245,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.309,"y":-2.581,"z":-0.001,"el":"C"},{"x":3.761,"y":-0.682,"z":0.036,"el":"C"},{"x":3.216,"y":-2.067,"z":-0.226,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.837,"y":-0.767,"z":0.001,"el":"C"},{"x":3.418,"y":1.821,"z":0.196,"el"